@@ -3,3 +3,24 @@
 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+## JSON Pointer (RFC 6901)
+
+`resolvePointer(document, pointer)` returns the value of `document` that the JSON Pointer `pointer`
+refers to.
+
+```ts
+import { resolvePointer } from "./src/index.ts";
+
+resolvePointer({ foo: ["bar", "baz"] }, "/foo/1"); // "baz"
+resolvePointer({ "a/b": 1 }, "/a~1b"); // 1 (`~1` is `/`, `~0` is `~`)
+resolvePointer(doc, ""); // doc itself
+```
+
+- Throws a `SyntaxError` when the pointer is not a valid JSON Pointer (it must be empty or start with `/`,
+  and `~` must be followed by `0` or `1`), and an `Error` when it does not resolve: missing member,
+  array index out of range or with a leading zero, the `-` end marker, or descending into a scalar.
+- Only own members are followed (no prototype-chain access); the document is never mutated.
+- The URI fragment representation (RFC 6901 section 6) is not supported.
+
+Run the tests with `npm test`.
diff --git a/src/index.ts b/src/index.ts
